            "review_title": "Review at Tempura Kubara",
            "review_text": "Quan\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam159 contributions\n0\nGood Tempura but a bit pricy\nMar 2018 • Couples\nThere's a tempera and katsu restaurant craze everywhere so I wanted to try it out. See if I can learn what science and art is around frying battered foods. It's good, better than most tempura. Light batter and fresh quality ingredients. Still it's fried and a bit oily taking time to dry. Had the same issue with katsu specialized restaurants in past. Service was great, very Japanese gentle and polite. But in the end I don't know how I can justify the price. It's just too much for some fried foods that is well presented.\nRead more\nWritten March 10, 2018",
